    "details": "<p>All that you need to know about the 24-Hour Hardware Hackathon</p>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Theme:&nbsp; </strong>Experience Innovation</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">The 24-Hour Hardware Hackathon returns with the theme \"Experience Innovation\" a call to participants to move beyond ideas on paper and construct real, working solutions to real-world problems within a single, time-bound sprint.</li>\n</ul>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Domains:</strong></div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Intelligent &amp; Autonomous Systems</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Energy &amp; Sustainable Technologies</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">AI &amp; Healthcare Technologies</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Smart Infrastructure &amp; Digital Ecosystems</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Resilience &amp; Emerging Technologies</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Open Innovation</li>\n</ul>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Guidelines:</strong></div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Team Size:</strong> Teams must consist of 2 to 4 members.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Inter-college Team Members:</strong> Allowed (encouraged to promote collaborative innovation).</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Cross-Domain Team Members:</strong> Allowed (encouraged for multidisciplinary approaches).</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Idea Submission:</strong> Participants are expected to submit innovative hardware solutions addressing challenges within the provided domains.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Selection</strong>: Teams will be shortlisted based on their idea submission in ppt.</li>\n</ul>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Event Format:</strong></div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Round 1: Online Idea Submission on Unstop.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Round 2: 24-Hour continuous on-campus hardware hackathon for the shortlisted teams <strong>(convergence pass is mandatory for every shortlisted team member)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Process &amp; Timeline:</strong></div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Round 1 (Idea Submission):</strong></div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Teams must submit their innovative idea detailing the problem statement, proposed solution, technical approach, feasibility, and expected impact.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Deadline:</strong> September 13th, 11:59 PM.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Shortlisted teams Announcement:</strong> September 15th.</li>\n</ul>\n<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>Round 2 (On-Campus Finale):</strong>&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">The shortlisted teams will build and demonstrate their working hardware prototypes on campus.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Convergence Pass is mandatory for all the team members.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\"><strong>Date: </strong>18th - 19th September</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participation Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\">All participating teams must bring their own laptops and all necessary hardware components required for their prototype.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">The project must be developed during the hackathon period. Use of pre-built prototypes is prohibited.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Teams must be present for all designated mentorship and evaluation rounds to remain eligible for the event.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Ethical use of AI tools and publicly available resources is permitted.</li>\n<li dir=\"auto\">Participants must adhere to the venue's code of conduct and maintain professional behavior throughout the 24-hour event.</li>\n</ul>",
